## Filament JSON / YAML Editor (asignua/filament-json-yaml-editor)

- Form fields: `Asignua\FilamentJsonYamlEditor\Forms\JsonEditor` and `Forms\YamlEditor`. The wire state is always TEXT; by default the model gets the text back. `->asArray()` makes the form hand the model a decoded array; without it the field follows the model cast (`array`/`json`/`object`/`collection`/`AsArrayObject`/`AsCollection` get an array automatically, `->asArray(false)` forces text; pass `->asArray()` explicitly outside a model). An array/Collection/object coming from the model is always shown as text. Blank text is stored as `null`. With `->asArray()` the syntax rule stays even after `->validateSyntax(false)`; YAML timestamps stay ISO strings, `{}` stays an object.
- `JsonEditor` options: `->modes([EditorMode::Code, EditorMode::Tree])`, `->defaultMode()`, `->format(bool)` (Format button), `->indent(int)`, `->height('24rem'|px)`, `->wrapLines()`, `->onlyContainers()`, `->validateSyntax(false)`, `->schema($schema)`. Editing in the tree view re-serialises the document with `JSON.stringify`: integer-like keys are re-ordered and numbers beyond 2^53 lose precision; expanding/collapsing nodes and the code view never change the text.
- `YamlEditor` options: `->inline(int)` (nesting level where `Yaml::dump` switches to flow style), `->indent(int)`, `->dumpFlags(int)`, `->height()`, `->wrapLines()`, `->validateSyntax(false)`, `->schema($schema)` (validates the parsed document). Comments survive only while the state stays text: `->asArray()` drops them.
- The syntax rule is added automatically: `Rules\JsonRule` (`->containerOnly()`, depth), `Rules\YamlRule` (symfony/yaml, no object instantiation). `Rules\JsonSchemaRule::make($schema)->yaml()` needs `opis/json-schema` (preferred) or `justinrainbow/json-schema`; with neither it throws a `LogicException` instead of passing silently. With justinrainbow, remote and `file://` `$ref`s are refused (only bundled draft meta-schemas resolve). YAML whose aliases expand past a budget fails `YamlRule`.
- Infolists: `Infolists\JsonEntry` / `Infolists\YamlEntry` (Phiki highlighting, `->collapsible()`, `->collapsed()`, `->maxHeight()`, `->summary()`, `->copyable()` is on by default). State may be an array, an object or text.
- Assets: run `php artisan filament:assets` after install/update. The editor bundle loads only on pages that render an editor.
